{
  "doc": [
    "twoody/vault/device-access/v2 (docs/mesh-design.md §1 rule 5). Reference: src/vault/contracts.ts (signDeviceAccessV2, deviceAccessV2Valid, deviceAccessUsable). Replaces v1, which named no computer and never expired: only v2 is accepted.",
    "A person-device (the phone, or a Desktop) states with its own vault signing key that a tunnel key is its own, for ONE account computer, until `exp`: that computer then links it without the account token deciding anything (rule 5), or, when the request is let in by rule 1 (the device that added the computer), knows which vault device it is (who may pin itself as the computer's vault anchor, seal turns, reach the other computers' documents).",
    "Signature scheme: Ed25519 (RFC 8032) by the private half of the vault device's sign_public, over the canonical header: UTF-8 of the label 'twoody/vault/device-access/v2', then for each field the UTF-8 of String(field) prefixed by its byte length on 2 bytes big-endian. Fields: [v, user_id, vault_device_id, tunnel_public_key, account_computer_id, exp] with v = '2'.",
    "Field encodings: user_id decimal ('42'); vault_device_id the signer's vault_devices uuid; tunnel_public_key the requester's X25519 tunnel key, 64 lowercase hex (the key it asks with); account_computer_id the account_computers id of the computer asked (as request_access names it); exp Unix time in SECONDS, an integer (decimal in the statement, a JSON number on the wire). Signature: 128 lowercase hex.",
    "Wire form (request_access's device_access, passed on by the account): {vault_device_id, tunnel_public_key, account_computer_id, exp, signature}. Verifiers refuse it unless: tunnel_public_key equals the key the request asks with; account_computer_id is the verifier's own account computer; now < exp <= now + 86400 (at most 24 h ahead: sign a fresh one per request); the signer is a trusted person-device of the verified roster (rule 5) — the signature checked with that roster entry's sign_public, never a key the statement brings.",
    "Keys: those of device-access-v1.json (same devices); the Pi's account computer id is 9f3d5b72-4c6e-4a8f-8b2d-3e5f7a9b1c22."
  ],
